.lattice/story/actives/B-137a/review-passes.json:2153:      "note": "Concept deletion/replacement residue review of the story-level integrated change (git diff main...HEAD): no blocker. Zero files deleted or renamed (--diff-filter=D and --diff-filter=R -M both empty), so all analysis is on in-file symbol/vocabulary removals. Five concept deletions/replacements identified and each verified residue-free. (1) Host-run slot registry relocated to core/provider-process-registry.ts: the 8 removed exports (acquireHostRunSlot, hostRunSlotsDir, releaseSlot, resolveMaxConcurrent, resolveSlotStaleMs, scanLiveSlots, writeSlotFileExclusive, HOST_RUN_MAX_CONCURRENT_DEFAULT) plus AcquiredHostRunSlot/HostRunLiveDescriptor all resolve to an explicitly-commented \"Deprecated compatibility aliases\" block at core/host-run.ts:425-440 that re-exports the canonical implementations and names provider-process-registry as exclusive owner of ownership/reclaim semantics, satisfying this lane's backward-compat-with-comment exemption; provider-process-registry-smoke.ts:460 mechanically asserts host-run.ts retains no second slot registry. Removed internals isSlotReclaimable, sameSlotOccupant, readSlotOccupant and SlotOccupant survive only inside the new canonical registry, i.e. a clean move with no orphaned callers. (2) Slot directory rename .lattice/usage/host-run-slots/ -> .lattice/runtime/provider-process-slots/ (PROVIDER_PROCESS_SLOTS_RELATIVE, provider-process-registry.ts:30): zero residual references in live source, docs or config; the only remaining occurrence is the negative-control assertion at proof-admissibility-registry-smoke.ts:292, and the surviving old-path strings in .lattice/story/actives/B-70e9/{plan.md,delivery-check.json} are frozen artifacts of a different story, not residue of this diff. (3) DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MINUTES replaced by exported CROSS_HOST_REVIEW_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=12 (handlers/cross-host-review.ts:54), preserving the protected cross_host_review.maxRuntimeMinutes