deadlineAt, workerHeartbeatAt, lastProviderProgressAt, providerProgressMode, managedReview, absolute_deadline_exceeded, legacy_unmanaged, evidenceCommandTimeoutOverrides) resolves to real non-test implementation in packages/main/src. No doc-promise-undelivered case found. Canonical reports read via node bin/lattice.js and reported honestly, not consumed as gate evidence and not upgraded: acceptance_topology_check status=inconclusive structuralPass=false blocking=false mode=observe authority=diagnostic_only (AT_UNMAPPED_SCOPE_REF, AT_MISSING_TOPOLOGY); pre_review_check_read status=inconclusive ok=false blocking=false mode=observe authority=inadmissible (PR_ARTIFACT_TAMPERED, PR_NEW_PATH_UNMAPPED, PR_COVERAGE_BASIS_CHANGED, PR_COVERAGE_INCONCLUSIVE, PR_POSITIVE_EVIDENCE_MISSING, PR_PRODUCTION_PATH_UNPROVEN, PR_MUTATION_EVIDENCE_MISSING, PR_MUTATION_DID_NOT_BITE and others); acceptance_rollout_report_read status=fail ok=false blocking=false mode=observe receipt=stale quorum=full-3x2; acceptance_rollout_check status=fail ok=false blocking=false mode=observe receipt=stale quorum=full-3x2. All four are non-PASS in observe mode with blocking=false and this work makes no promotion claim, so under the stated policy they are advisory only for this lane; no topology fabricated and no degraded 3x1 accepted. Scope-honesty note: the dispatch prompt recorded a SHADOW candidate-routing escalation (candidate_cutoff_tie plus missing_protected_source for docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md, core/managed-host-run.ts, core/managed-review-evidence.ts and handlers/managed-review-evidence.ts); those files all exist on this branch and were inspected directly, and per the prompt instruction the escalation was treated as non-gate evidence and did not limit this review.",
