.lattice/story/actives/B-137a/review-passes.json:2283:      "note": "Docs-code consistency review for B-137a: no blockers. Step 1 extracted ~1485 changed declarations from git diff main...HEAD, of which ~160 are newly exported symbols (managed-host-run.ts, managed-review-evidence.ts, provider-process-registry.ts, provider-process-admission.ts, native-review-*.ts). Step 2 identified 6 changed doc surfaces referencing those symbols: docs/host-run-usage.md (+322/-107), new docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md (255 lines), docs/CLI.md, and 3 modified decision docs (multi-host-keyword-candidate-spec-routing, session-ownership-and-write-leases, tier-c-crosshost-quorum). Step 3 compared roughly 20 doc paragraphs against the new code. Forward scan (code->docs) found every documented constant matches source: 30s waitMs cap (MANAGED_HOST_RUN_STATUS_WAIT_MAX_MS), 30min default / 24h max deadline, 90d retention, 8 MiB output ceiling, concurrency cap default 4 (PROVIDER_PROCESS_MAX_CONCURRENT_DEFAULT), 6h stale backstop. Runtime paths (.lattice/runtime/host-runs/, host-run-receipts/, host-run-prompts/, provider-process-slots/) match, and the retired .lattice/usage/host-run-slots/ path was correctly removed. CLI surface matches command-catalog.ts: host_run --detach/--deadlineMs/--managedReview, host_run_status, host_run_cancel, host_run_worker (visibility:'internal', matching the doc's 'hidden from ordinary help/catalog discovery'), managed_review_evidence_import accepting only runId+receiptId with no verdict override. Claude managed_reviewer launch claims verified against host-run.ts:1594-1630 (0600 one-shot prompt under provider cwd, --permission-mode bypassPermissions and --json-schema scoped to that profile only, ordinary runs keep configured policy, Codex keeps stdin transport). Import gate replacementSafe && reaped && !residualProcessGroup verified at managed-review-evidence.ts:379-381. 'doctor --full' phrasing verified correct: the per-run listing is gated on !brief in renderManagedHostRunDoctorSection and doctor is brief-by-default per BRIEF_DEFAULT_CLI_COMMANDS. Reverse scan (docs->code, closing self-check) found no doc-promise-undelivered: every concrete lattice command named in the changed docs is registered in the catalog (remaining grep misses were namespace prefixes like 'lattice host run'); all 10 LATTICE_* env vars named in the docs are read by code, with both new ones (LATTICE_HOST_RUN_MAX_CONCURRENT, LATTICE_HOST_RUN_SLOT_STALE_MS) resolving in provider-process-registry.ts:173-187 at the documented defaults; the new validate.evidenceCommandTimeoutOverrides paragraph in CLI.md matches resolveEvidenceCommandTimeoutMs (validation-executor.ts:550-575) exactly on exact executable+ordered-argv identity, allowlisted executable, and fail-closed-to-270s default on malformed rows or duplicate identities; the dispatch 'two execution modes' promise is delivered at story-dispatch.ts:177-180. The cap-lowering paragraph was rewritten in this diff from 'new admissions only try the lowered range' to 'counts every live high-index slot and refuses new starts until the total live count drops below the new cap' -- I verified the NEW wording is the accurate one (acquireProviderProcessSlot calls directory-wide scanLiveProviderProcessSlotsUnlocked and refuses on live.length >= boundedCap), so this is a correct repair rather than drift. Agy retirement is consistently applied across synopsis, host enum, usage-parsing table and decision docs, with the pre-spawn fail-closed refusal accurately documented (host-run.ts:1630) and the historical agy-cli artifact union retained as read-only backward compatibility. Canonical reports read and reported honestly, all advisory not blocking: acceptance_topology_check = inconclusive/basis partial/authority diagnostic_only/blocking=no; pre_review_check_read = FAIL PR_ARTIFACT_TAMPERED, mode=observe/blocking=false; acceptance_rollout_report_read = FAIL AR_REPORT_STALE; acceptance_rollout_check = FAIL AR_REPORT_STALE, mode=observe/blocking=false/promotionEligible=false. None asserts blocking=true, project mode is observe not enforce, and this work makes no promotion claim, so per the role contract these are advisory only and were neither fabricated nor upgraded to a formal pass. No documentation-code inconsistencies found.",
