.lattice/story/actives/B-137a/review-passes.json:2344:      "note": "Test-coverage review PASS for B-137a. Coverage: 58 must-priority verificationIntents across CHK-001..CHK-007 (7/7/8/8/8/12/8), 58 verificationEvidence rows, 0 must-gaps, 0 waivers, 0 result=fail. Every intent maps to exactly one distinct intentRef; no orphan or duplicate refs. All 11 cited task files exist in packages/main/src/tasks and are built under packages/main/dist/tasks. I executed the cited evidence rather than trusting recorded results: managed-host-run-smoke PASS, managed-host-run-command-smoke PASS, managed-host-run-process-smoke PASS, managed-host-run-e2e-smoke PASS, managed-review-evidence-smoke PASS, provider-process-registry-smoke PASS (incl. provider-launch-owner-admission-suite), proof-admissibility-registry-smoke PASS, cross-host-review-smoke PASS (27 checks). Assertions are substantive rather than name-matching: controller verdict-override/impersonation/severity-downgrade refusals (managed-review-evidence-smoke:1112,1242,2275), process-group TERM->KILL->reap with residualProcessGroup=false and replacementSafe=false under PID/PGID fingerprint ambiguity (managed-host-run-process-smoke:109,148,288,335), silent-but-live provider held running past the legacy ten-minute observation boundary with completionRunnerCalls=1 proving no duplicate spawn (managed-host-run-smoke:338-341,1198-1210), and negative controls (e.g. F-102 launch-fence GRANTED assertion) that fail loudly instead of silently testing the wrong branch. managed-cross-provider-suite-smoke is a genuine fail-closed aggregator over 8 child smokes. HARNESS ARTIFACTS, NOT DEFECTS (deliberately not filed as findings): (1) proof-admissibility-registry-smoke exits rc=1 under this reviewer environment because LATTICE_AGENT leaks my dispatched role lattice-review-test-coverage into the spawned mutant child, so agent_dispatch_mutation_denied fires in the dispatch registry before the intake evaluator boundary can bite the valid=true mut