    B-137a: complete the F-127 fix — imported evidence stays verifiable after GC

    The earlier commit only stopped the crash; post-GC verification of an imported
    pass still refused. Completed here, after settling the design question the
    previous commit deferred.

    The deferral assumed archiving the proposal would widen what GC retains on a
    security-critical path. Measurement showed otherwise. The sensitive bulk GC exists
    to shed is live-output.jsonl (923 KB observed) and result.json's
    finalAssistantResult (6.7 KB of raw provider text) — both still deleted. What
    verification actually needs is structured VERDICT metadata carrying no provider
    transcript: evidence-proposal.json (6.8 KB: conclusion, lane, providerAgent,
    reviewRunId, readManifest/readLog provenance) plus the 550-byte import-seal pair
    (runId / receiptId / storyId / reviewRunId / lane / importedAt / importedIds). So
    the doc's "Retained output may contain sensitive provider text" concern and full
    re-verifiability are not in conflict.

    Archived, each captured BEFORE removeManagedHostRunRuntime deletes it:
      - the binding projection (previous commit)
      - the proposal RAW TEXT — the sealed evidenceProposalDigest is sha256 over file
        bytes, so a re-serialized object would not re-digest identically
      - the import-seal pair, via the new archive-backed readManagedReviewImportSeal

    Integrity is NOT relaxed. Every archived body is re-digested on read against the
    sealed receipt's evidenceProposalDigest / the archive's evidenceBindingDigest, and
    a missing spec.json distinguishes a genuinely reclaimed run from an absent artifact
    on a live one. Negative controls confirm it: authentic archives verify, while
    flipping the proposal's conclusion pass->fail or rewriting the seal's runId is
    REJECTED, not trusted.

    End-to-end on a real imported pass in an isolated copy of the runtime root:
    pre-GC valid=true, post-GC valid=true (was valid=false with eight reason codes).

    Regression coverage extended where the defect hid: managed-host-run-smoke's GC
    block asserted only that the RECEIPT stayed auditable, never that imported
    evidence stayed VERIFIABLE. It now asserts all three archive-backed reads.
    Mutation-proven — dropping evidenceProposalText or evidenceBindingText fails it.

    managed-review-evidence-smoke PASS, managed-host-run-smoke PASS,
    managed-cross-provider-suite-smoke PASS.

