exact signed invocation attestation. Native lifecycle remains owned by the host.\n- Native host without that broker integration is advisory-only and cannot write formal finding/pass evidence; use the managed reviewer path below instead.\n- Cross-provider CLI reviewer: do not launch raw `bash + codex/claude/agy`. The controller first starts review_run_start, then submits the exact run through ManagedHostRun:\n  lattice host_run '{\"host\":\"codex\",\"storyId\":\"B-137a\",\"agentType\":\"lattice-review-docs\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"lane\":\"lattice-review-docs\",\"managedReview\":true,\"detach\":true,\"json\":true}'\n  Poll the returned runId with `lattice host_run_status '{\"runId\":\"<runId>\",\"afterGeneration\":<generation>,\"waitMs\":30000,\"json\":true}'`. A 30-second return or provider silence is not failure and never authorizes a replacement.\n  The provider final assistant result must be exactly one bounded `lattice.managed_review_final_proposal.v1` JSON envelope. The managed adapter seals the strictly validated verdict; the controller cannot supply or override it.\n  Only after state=completed and an exact receiptId exists, call `lattice managed_review_evidence_import '{\"runId\":\"<runId>\",\"receiptId\":\"<receiptId>\"}'`.\n- A raw provider CLI result is manual/advisory output only; it cannot satisfy the managed reviewer evidence path.\n\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Native path: start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-137a\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-docs\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId. In the managed cross-provider path the controller already performed this step.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-137a\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-docs\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-docs\ndescription: REVIEW review: documentation-code consistency (narrowed input: only review documentation sections referenced by symbols changed in the diff)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing first-stage check)\n\nAfter completing all Steps 1-3 below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?**\n\nSpecific checks:\n- New `lattice <cmd>` examples added in CLAUDE.md / README → check the code for a corresponding handler registration (does registry.ts import + registerBatch)\n- New fields added to handler schema → check whether the docs have corresponding descriptions\n- New ENV variables / config options added → check whether the docs have a corresponding section\n- New behavior description paragraphs added → check whether the code has a corresponding implementation\n\nIf you find \"docs promised but code didn't deliver\" → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`). This is a reverse check — Steps 1-3 are a code→docs forward scan, this section is a docs→code reverse scan.\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou do only one thing: check whether the docs (README*.md / CLAUDE.md / docs/\\*\\*/\\*.md) and the code (exported symbols changed in git diff main...HEAD) are consistent.\n\n**Do not scan the entire README / CLAUDE.md**; only look at the paragraphs in the docs that reference the symbols changed in this diff. Narrowing the input is a hard requirement, not an optimization suggestion.\n\n## Procedure\n\n### Step 1: Extract the symbol list (function names / class names / constants) from git diff\n\n```bash\n# Extract the exported symbols changed in this story. Regex matches common