ted terminal and evidence artifacts, and post-claim runtime files; prompt and capability plaintext must not appear in argv or durable receipts, one-shot inputs must be mode 0600 and removed after claim, and only bounded redacted projections or digests may remain.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Supply unknown, malformed, path-traversal, cross-project, or stale runId values to status and cancel; commands must reject without reading or mutating another run and without spawning any provider process.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"logic\"},{\"desc\":\"Kill the foreground attaching caller while its managed worker is active, then attach from a new caller; the original run must remain observable and complete once, proving CLI watchdog runtimeContinuation cannot translate caller loss into provider cancellation.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:2\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Exercise waitMs at 0, 30000, and above 30000 plus a no-change interval; every call is bounded, values above the cap are rejected or capped explicitly, and a wait timeout reports the current non-terminal state without treating it as provider failure.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Call host_run_cancel repeatedly before claim, during execution, and after terminal completion; cancellation is idempotent, targets only the original run, and never creates a second terminal or changes an already authoritative terminal outcome.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:1\",\"priority\":\"must\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Detached host_run returns only after the worker claim handshake with runId, running state, and deadlineAt; host_run_status --waitMs 30000 then long-polls that same identity and returns progress or its terminal receipt, while foreground host_run is submit-and-attach over the identical durable run.\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"